# Expo/React Native's Metro bundler requires a single, deduplicated copy of
# react/react-native/expo's own packages across the whole workspace — pnpm's
# default isolated node_modules can otherwise resolve `expo` against two
# different peer-dependency contexts and install it (and react/react-native)
# twice, which expo-doctor flags as a real risk of duplicate-native-module
# crashes at runtime. A public-hoist-pattern alone wasn't enough to prevent
# the split; a fully hoisted/flat node_modules (npm/yarn-classic style) is
# Expo's own documented fix for pnpm monorepos.
# See https://docs.expo.dev/guides/monorepos/ and https://expo.fyi/resolving-dependency-issues
node-linker=hoisted
